From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:42:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] WebAssembly port: the layer common to every WebAssembly
 build

What any WebAssembly build of ooRexx needs, whatever the toolchain:
Emscripten (the browser and Node, next patch) or WASI (any WASI runtime).
CMakeLists.txt defines ORX_WASM for both (and ORX_WASI for WASI); the code
is under #if defined(ORX_WASM); native builds are unchanged.

- static librexx (linked --whole-archive, so the _rexx_init() constructor
  that creates the interpreter locks is kept) and librexxapi; no IPO (with
  LTO the final code generation loses -fwasm-exceptions, and every catch);
- the API server (queues, registrations, macrospace) linked in and reached
  in-process (SysLoopbackConnection), so registered functions resolve as
  natively (RxFuncAdd of classic library functions,
  RexxRegisterFunctionExe);
- rxregexp, rxmath and hostemu embedded in the interpreter
  (PackageManager::embeddedPackages; no dlopen), and rxsock and rxunixsys
  too under Emscripten;
- other libraries a build links in described by a table SysLibrary looks
  up instead of dlopen/dlsym (orx_wasm_static_libraries(), a weak symbol:
  absent in the standard builds), so "LIBRARY name", RxFuncAdd() and the
  Rexx*Dll() registrations find them unchanged;
- rexxc, rxqueue and rxsubcom in the rexx executable (multi-call:
  rexx --orx-wasm-TOOL), and more tools a build links in
  (orxWasmExtraTool(), weak);
- errno values seen by Rexx programs (RC of CD, stream ERROR:n, SysMkDir,
  SysFileDelete, ...) mapped from the WASI numbers of the WebAssembly
  libcs to the Linux ones (HOST_ERRNO; the identity on every other
  platform);
- orxWasmSignal(), exported: what the native signal handler does for
  SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP (a HALT in every activity; a SysSleep ends at
  once, EINTR), for the host to call when it gets one;
- what the interpreter asks of its host goes through the host functions of
  common/platform/unix/SysWasmHost.hpp, weak symbols a runtime defines when
  it has the facility: external commands (orxWasmCommandRun() and the
  collected output; without them, commands fail closed, RC 127, after CD,
  EXPORT and the others the interpreter handles itself) and the paths of
  .RexxInfo~executable and ~libraryPath.
